WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.405
Inside the cluster, every pod can call every other pod.

2
00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:06.605
A namespace is a folder for names.

3
00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:08.440
It is not a firewall.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:14.465
This port has three steps: see the flat network, deny by default, and allow DNS.

5
00:00:14.485 --> 00:00:16.600
First: close every door.

6
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.738
One policy selects every pod and allows nothing.

7
00:00:19.758 --> 00:00:22.360
Now all inbound traffic is blocked.

8
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.910
Then you add one small rule for each real path.

9
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.620
For example: web to API.

10
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.445
Rules select pods by label.

11
00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:31.695
And the rules add up.

12
00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:34.305
Second: block outbound traffic too.

13
00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:35.755
You deny all egress.

14
00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:38.240
And then every call by name fails.

15
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.577
So allow the cluster DNS on port 53 first.

16
00:00:41.597 --> 00:00:44.490
Then open what each app needs.

17
00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.925
Quick recap of network policies.

18
00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:48.137
Deny by default.

19
00:00:48.157 --> 00:00:49.525
Allow each real path.

20
00:00:49.545 --> 00:00:51.510
And never forget DNS.

21
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.630
Now start the first lesson below.
